```
import java.util.*;
public class SortAndRemoveDuplicates {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Integer> numbers = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(2, 3, 5, 8, 6, 4));
        Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>(numbers);
        numbers.clear();
        numbers.addAll(set);
        Collections.sort(numbers);
        System.out.println(numbers);
    }
}
```
In this code, we first create an ArrayList of the given numbers. Then, we create a HashSet from this ArrayList to remove duplicates. We clear the ArrayList and add the elements from the HashSet back to the ArrayList to get a list of unique numbers. Finally, we sort the ArrayList using the Collections.sort() method and print the sorted list.

