How can I implement a function in Swift that can determine if a given string contains a specific substring? Can you provide an example usage of the function in Swift code using a Mark down syntax?
Here's an example implementation of the function in Swift that is case-insensitive:
```swift
func contains(_ str: String, _ substr: String) -> Bool {
    return str.range(of: substr, options: .caseInsensitive) != nil
}
```
To use this function, simply call it and pass in the string and substring as arguments:
```swift
let string = "Hello, world!"
if contains(string, "hello") {
    print("The string contains 'hello'.")
} else {
    print("The string does not contain 'hello'.")
}
```
This will output "The string contains 'hello'." because the `contains` function is case-insensitive and will match the lowercase "hello" in the string.

