2. We prompt the user to enter a string using `fmt.Print()` and read the input using `fmt.Scanln()`.
3. We convert the input string to a `[]rune` slice using the `[]rune()` function. This is necessary because Go strings are immutable, so we can't modify them directly.
4. We use one loop to swap the first and last runes, then the second and second-to-last runes, and so on until we reach the middle of the slice. We do this by using the `len()` function to get the length of the slice and dividing it by 2 to get the midpoint. We then use the loop variable `i` to index into the slice, swapping the `i`th and `len(runes)-1-i`th runes on each iteration.
